# ---------------------------------------------------------------- secrets
.env
*.env

# ------------------------------------------------------------- real people
# Spreadsheets and client documents are blocked by extension rather than by
# name, so a new export dropped into the folder is ignored by default instead
# of being committed by accident. The repository is shared; once real staff
# data is in history it cannot be taken back out.
#
# The pipeline reads teams.csv from SharePoint at runtime (_config/teams.csv).
# It was never meant to be version controlled.
*.csv
*.docx
*.xlsx
phone_list.txt
.zoom_directory.json
client_docs/

# Documentation is generated as a PDF and is meant to ship.
*.pdf
!docs/*.pdf

# ------------------------------------------------------- tenant identifiers
# Site and drive ids for the client's tenant. Rebuilt automatically on the
# first run, so there is nothing to gain by committing it.
.site.json

# ------------------------------------------------------------ runtime state
# Written while the pipeline runs. In production all of this lives in
# STATE_DIR on the Azure Files share, never in the working copy.
queue/
*.log
failures.log
.backfill_progress.json
.processed.json
state.db

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ local
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.~lock.*
.DS_Store

# One-off tool that built the first teams.csv from the client handout.
# Its inputs (phone_list.txt, teams_TEMPLATE.csv) are ignored above, so it
# cannot run from a clone, and it has real staff names hardcoded in it.
# Kept on disk beside those inputs, deliberately not committed.
build_team_map.py

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ tests
# The repository carries the production code only. The suites and their
# synthetic fixtures stay on the development machine.
test_*.py
fixtures/
